            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P1 · Application availability — error budget burn (fast)\n**WHAT:** Error budget for Application availability is being consumed 14.4× faster than sustainable, confirmed over 1h and still true over the last 5m.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `application-platform` (application / slo, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customer-facing objective at risk. At the current rate the 30d budget is exhausted well before the window ends.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Multi-window burn rate: the long window (1h) proves the burn is sustained rather than a spike, and the short window (5m) means it is still happening now. Both must be true, which is what makes burn-rate alerting both fast and quiet.\n**OWNER:** sre · support 24x7 · this pages the on-call rotation\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `SLO Error Budget Burn` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-major-incident` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `application-platform.prod.application-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-app-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Application availability — error budget burn (fast) — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P1.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Application availability — error budget burn (fast) — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Application availability — error budget burn (fast)\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-app-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
