            "id": "314408958",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P1 · Deployment-Induced Customer Impact — CONFIRMED\n**WHAT:** The single highest-precision page in the framework: an error-rate regression AND a latency regression in the same service within the post-deploy window. Almost never a false positive, and the remediation is known before a human reads the alert (roll back).\n**WHY THIS IS DIFFERENT:** every member condition below is true at the same time, which is what separates a real incident from an isolated symptom:\n  - Deployment Regression\n  - API p99 Latency Degradation\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod`\n**SERVICE / SCOPE:** `application-platform` (application)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Confirmed impact: every member condition is true simultaneously, which is the evidence threshold this platform requires before paging on a symptom.\n**OWNER:** application-development (observers: sre) · pages the on-call rotation\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Treat as a confirmed incident. The member alerts are the evidence trail; the runbook's remediation section applies directly.\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Deployment Regression` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-enrich-change`.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-app-availability`\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Deployment-Induced Customer Impact\nAt least one member condition cleared, so the confirmed-impact state no longer holds. Individual member monitors may still be alerting — check before closing the incident.\n{{/is_recovery}}",
