            "id": "314408966",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P1 · Redundancy Loss With Confirmed Availability Impact — CONFIRMED\n**WHAT:** An instance disappearing is normal in an elastic estate. An instance disappearing while the deployment can no longer serve its declared replica count is a real loss of redundancy.\n**WHY THIS IS DIFFERENT:** every member condition below is true at the same time, which is what separates a real incident from an isolated symptom:\n  - Kubernetes Deployment Redundancy Degraded\n  - Pods in CrashLoopBackOff\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod`\n**SERVICE / SCOPE:** `kubernetes-platform` (kubernetes)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Confirmed impact: every member condition is true simultaneously, which is the evidence threshold this platform requires before paging on a symptom.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · pages the on-call rotation\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Treat as a confirmed incident. The member alerts are the evidence trail; the runbook's remediation section applies directly.\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Kubernetes Deployment Redundancy Degraded` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-k8s-workload`.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-k8s-workload-availability`\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Redundancy Loss With Confirmed Availability Impact\nAt least one member condition cleared, so the confirmed-impact state no longer holds. Individual member monitors may still be alerting — check before closing the incident.\n{{/is_recovery}}",
