        {
          "index_key": "custom.prod.checkout-payment-authorization-rate",
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "assets": [
              {
                "category": "runbook",
                "name": "API Availability",
                "resource_key": "15298344",
                "resource_type": "notebook",
                "url": "https://app.datadoghq.com/notebook/15298344"
              }
            ],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314408822",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P1 · Checkout Payment Authorization Rate\n**WHAT:** Payment authorization decline ratio has deviated from its learned baseline.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `checkout-api` (api / service, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customers cannot complete purchases. A decline-rate shift is usually an acquirer or issuer problem and is invisible to availability monitoring — every request succeeds with HTTP 200 while no money moves.\n\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** No catalog archetype models a business-outcome ratio. This is the single highest-value signal for the payments business and cannot be expressed as an infrastructure or golden-signal monitor.\n\n**OWNER:** payments · support 24x7 · this pages the on-call rotation\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `API Availability` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-api-health` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `checkout-api.prod.checkout-api` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-api-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Checkout Payment Authorization Rate — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P1.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Checkout Payment Authorization Rate — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Checkout Payment Authorization Rate\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-api-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "1",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P1][prod][api] Checkout Payment Authorization Rate (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 0,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "1",
            "query": "avg(last_15m):anomalies(sum:acme.payments.authorizations{env:prod,service:checkout-api,result:declined}.as_rate() / sum:acme.payments.authorizations{env:prod,service:checkout-api}.as_rate(), 'agile', 3, direction='above') \u003e= 1",
            "renotify_interval": 30,
            "renotify_occurrences": 3,
