            "id": "314408629",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P1 · API Availability\n**WHAT:** API Availability: availability signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `api-services` (api / service, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customers are affected now, or a mission-critical capability is unavailable.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** More than half of requests failing is an availability boundary, not a behavioral deviation. Sub-outage degradation is caught by the anomaly and burn-rate archetypes; this one exists to fire fast and unambiguously.\n\n**OWNER:** application-development · support 24x7 · this pages the on-call rotation\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `API Availability` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-api-health` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `api-services.prod.api-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-api-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## API Availability — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P1.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## API Availability — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · API Availability\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-api-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "0.5",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "0.2",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
