            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · API Latency Seasonal Anomaly\n**WHAT:** API Latency Seasonal Anomaly: latency signal detected by seasonal_anomaly analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `api-services` (api / service, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal deviated from its learned SEASONAL baseline (same hour, same day of week), so normal daily and weekly cycles are already accounted for.\n**OWNER:** application-development · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `API p99 Latency Degradation` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-api-health` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `api-services.prod.api-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-api-latency` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## API Latency Seasonal Anomaly — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## API Latency Seasonal Anomaly — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · API Latency Seasonal Anomaly\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-api-latency`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
