            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · API Management Capacity Saturation Forecast\n**WHAT:** Capacity is Azure's own composite of CPU, memory and queue depth for the gateway. Microsoft's guidance is to scale before sustained 70-80%, which is why this forecasts rather than alerts on the current value.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `api-services` (cloud / azure_apim, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Extrapolating the recent trend, this resource is projected to cross its limit inside the forecast horizon. It has not crossed it yet — that is the point.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `API Management Capacity Saturation Forecast` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-capacity-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `edge.prod.api-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-api-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## API Management Capacity Saturation Forecast — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## API Management Capacity Saturation Forecast — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · API Management Capacity Saturation Forecast\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-api-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "80",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "70",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][prod][cloud] API Management Capacity Saturation Forecast (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
              "subscription_name"
            ],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "max(next_12h):forecast(avg:azure.apimanagement_service.capacity{env:prod,alert_band:critical,resource_type:azure_apim} by {subscription_name,name}, 'linear', 1, interval='30m', history='1d') \u003e 80",
