            "id": "314986406",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · API Management Dependency Connectivity Degraded\n**WHAT:** API Management Dependency Connectivity Degraded: availability signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `api-services` (cloud / azure_apim, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Azure reports this as reachable (1) or not (0) per required dependency — storage, SQL, Key Vault. Anything below 1 means the gateway has lost a dependency it needs to start, configure or renew certificates, which surfaces later as a failure nobody connects back to networking.\n\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `API Management Dependency Connectivity Degraded` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-network` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `edge.prod.api-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-api-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## API Management Dependency Connectivity Degraded — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## API Management Dependency Connectivity Degraded — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · API Management Dependency Connectivity Degraded\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-api-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "1",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
