          "index_key": "prod.critical.cloud.azure-quota-exhaustion-forecast",
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "assets": [
              {
                "category": "runbook",
                "name": "Azure Subscription Quota Exhaustion Forecast",
                "resource_key": "15298388",
                "resource_type": "notebook",
                "url": "https://app.datadoghq.com/notebook/15298388"
              }
            ],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314408827",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Azure Subscription Quota Exhaustion Forecast\n**WHAT:** Quota exhaustion is the single most common cause of \"the deploy failed and nobody knows why\" in a large Azure estate. Quota increases take days, so the forecast window is a week.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `azure-landing-zone` (cloud / azure_subscription, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Extrapolating the recent trend, this resource is projected to cross its limit inside the forecast horizon. It has not crossed it yet — that is the point.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Azure Subscription Quota Exhaustion Forecast` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-capacity-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `cloud-quota.prod.azure-landing-zone` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-cloud-platform-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Azure Subscription Quota Exhaustion Forecast — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Azure Subscription Quota Exhaustion Forecast — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Azure Subscription Quota Exhaustion Forecast\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-cloud-platform-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "0.9",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "0.8",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][prod][cloud] Azure Subscription Quota Exhaustion Forecast (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
              "subscription_name"
            ],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "max(next_1w):forecast(avg:azure.usage.current_value{env:prod,alert_band:critical,resource_type:azure_subscription} by {subscription_name,quota_name} / avg:azure.usage.limit{env:prod,alert_band:critical,resource_type:azure_subscription} by {subscription_name,quota_name}, 'linear', 1, interval='60m', history='2w') \u003e 0.9",
            "renotify_interval": 30,
