            "id": "314986443",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Front Door WAF Block Surge\n**WHAT:** A block surge is either an attack or a WAF rule that just started rejecting legitimate traffic after a deployment. The second is far more common and far more damaging, which is why this is not routed as a security incident by default.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `security-telemetry` (cloud / azure_front_door, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal deviated from its own learned baseline by more than the configured number of deviations — not because it crossed a fixed number.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Front Door WAF Block Surge` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-security-control` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `edge.prod.security-telemetry` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-security-telemetry` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Front Door WAF Block Surge — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Front Door WAF Block Surge — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Front Door WAF Block Surge\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-security-telemetry`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
