            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · Redis Geo-Replication Unhealthy\n**WHAT:** Redis Geo-Replication Unhealthy: replication_lag signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `azure-landing-zone` (cloud / azure_redis, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Azure publishes geo-replication health as healthy (1) or not (0). Below 1 the secondary is no longer a usable failover target, which is the only reason it is being paid for.\n\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Redis Geo-Replication Unhealthy` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-azure-resource` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `caching.prod.azure-landing-zone` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-cloud-platform-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Redis Geo-Replication Unhealthy — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Redis Geo-Replication Unhealthy — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Redis Geo-Replication Unhealthy\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-cloud-platform-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
