            ],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314986577",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Traffic Manager Traffic Distribution Anomaly\n**WHAT:** Endpoints in one profile should receive comparable shares under weighted or performance routing. An endpoint diverging from its peers means either a routing-method change or a regional DNS problem that has not yet escalated to a failed probe.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `azure-landing-zone` (cloud / azure_traffic_manager, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** This member diverged from its peer group. Every peer receives the same work, so divergence is the defect.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Traffic Manager Traffic Distribution Anomaly` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-network` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `edge.prod.azure-landing-zone` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-cloud-platform-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Traffic Manager Traffic Distribution Anomaly — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Traffic Manager Traffic Distribution Anomaly — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Traffic Manager Traffic Distribution Anomaly\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-cloud-platform-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "0",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][prod][cloud] Traffic Manager Traffic Distribution Anomaly (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
              "name"
            ],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "avg(last_1h):outliers(sum:azure.network_trafficmanagerprofiles.qps_by_endpoint{env:prod,alert_band:critical,resource_type:azure_traffic_manager} by {name,endpoint_name}.as_rate(), 'DBSCAN', 3) \u003e 0",
