            "id": "314986434",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P1 · Cosmos DB Service Availability Degraded\n**WHAT:** Cosmos DB Service Availability Degraded: availability signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `database-platform` (database / azure_cosmos_db, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customers are affected now, or a mission-critical capability is unavailable.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** 99.99% is the Cosmos DB single-region SLA. Below it Microsoft is in breach of its own commitment, which is the point at which the correct action is to raise a support case rather than to keep investigating.\n\n**OWNER:** data-engineering · support 24x7 · this pages the on-call rotation\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Cosmos DB Service Availability Degraded` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-database` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `databases.prod.database-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-database-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Cosmos DB Service Availability Degraded — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P1.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Cosmos DB Service Availability Degraded — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Cosmos DB Service Availability Degraded\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-database-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "99.99",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "100",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P1][prod][database] Cosmos DB Service Availability Degraded (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
