            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · Snowflake Credit Consumption Anomaly\n**WHAT:** In Snowflake a credit spike is usually an engineering defect wearing a finance costume — a runaway query, a cross join, an auto-scale loop, or a warehouse someone forgot to auto-suspend.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `platform-services` (database / snowflake_warehouse, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal deviated from its own learned baseline by more than the configured number of deviations — not because it crossed a fixed number.\n**OWNER:** data-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Snowflake Credit Consumption Anomaly` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-finops-review` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `analytics.prod.platform-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-platform-services` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Snowflake Credit Consumption Anomaly — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Snowflake Credit Consumption Anomaly — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Snowflake Credit Consumption Anomaly\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-platform-services`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "1",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
