            "id": "314986482",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · SQL Server Buffer Pool Memory Pressure\n**WHAT:** Page life expectancy collapsing means the buffer pool is being churned — pages are evicted before they are reused, so reads go to disk. Measured as a fall against its own recent baseline because the healthy absolute value depends entirely on how much memory the instance has.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `database-platform` (database / sqlserver_instance, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal changed faster than the configured percentage relative to its own recent history. Speed of degradation, not absolute level.\n**OWNER:** data-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `SQL Server Buffer Pool Memory Pressure` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-database` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `databases.prod.database-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-database-latency` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## SQL Server Buffer Pool Memory Pressure — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## SQL Server Buffer Pool Memory Pressure — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · SQL Server Buffer Pool Memory Pressure\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-database-latency`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "-50",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "-30",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P2][prod][database] SQL Server Buffer Pool Memory Pressure (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "2",
            "query": "pct_change(avg(last_15m),last_4h):avg:sqlserver.buffer.page_life_expectancy{env:prod,alert_band:critical} by {host} \u003c -50",
