            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · SQL Server Restore Verification Stale\n**WHAT:** SQL Server Restore Verification Stale: backup_age signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `backup-platform` (database / sqlserver_instance, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** 168 hours is the weekly restore-test cycle the recovery standard commits to. Past it, the most recent PROOF of recoverability is more than a week old regardless of how fresh the backup files are.\n\n**OWNER:** data-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `SQL Server Restore Verification Stale` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-compliance-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `databases.prod.backup-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-infra-backup-success` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## SQL Server Restore Verification Stale — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## SQL Server Restore Verification Stale — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · SQL Server Restore Verification Stale\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-infra-backup-success`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
