            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · Critical OS Patches Missing\n**WHAT:** Critical OS Patches Missing: drift signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `security-telemetry` (infrastructure / host, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** A missing critical patch is a known exploitable defect with a published fix. There is no tolerance band to tune — the only question is how long it has been missing, which the runbook covers against the patch SLA.\n\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Critical OS Patches Missing` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-compliance-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `compute.prod.security-telemetry` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-security-telemetry` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Critical OS Patches Missing — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Critical OS Patches Missing — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Critical OS Patches Missing\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-security-telemetry`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
