            "id": "314986484",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · Operating System Past End of Life\n**WHAT:** Operating System Past End of Life: drift signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `security-telemetry` (infrastructure / host, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** 90 days is the shortest lead time in which an OS upgrade can realistically be planned, tested and rolled through an estate. After end of life there are no security patches at all, so the drift monitors above go quiet precisely when the risk is highest — which is why this one exists separately.\n\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Operating System Past End of Life` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-compliance-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `compute.prod.security-telemetry` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-security-telemetry` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Operating System Past End of Life — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Operating System Past End of Life — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Operating System Past End of Life\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-security-telemetry`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
