            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Event Hubs Capture Backlog\n**WHAT:** Event Hubs Capture Backlog: freshness signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `data-platform` (messaging / stream, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Capture writes events to storage on a fixed window. A sustained backlog means the archive is falling behind the stream, so the durable copy the data platform reads from is incomplete.\n\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Event Hubs Capture Backlog` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-data-pipeline` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `messaging.prod.data-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-data-freshness` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Event Hubs Capture Backlog — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Event Hubs Capture Backlog — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Event Hubs Capture Backlog\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-data-freshness`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
