            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P1 · ExpressRoute BGP Session Down\n**WHAT:** ExpressRoute BGP Session Down: availability signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `network-platform` (network / network_circuit, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customers are affected now, or a mission-critical capability is unavailable.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** BGP availability is published per peering as a percentage where anything below 100 means a session on one of the redundant links is down. The pair exists precisely so that one failure is survivable — and precisely so that one failure must be fixed before the second one arrives.\n\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support 24x7 · this pages the on-call rotation\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `ExpressRoute BGP Session Down` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-network` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `connectivity.prod.network-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-network-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## ExpressRoute BGP Session Down — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P1.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## ExpressRoute BGP Session Down — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · ExpressRoute BGP Session Down\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-network-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "100",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P1][prod][network] ExpressRoute BGP Session Down (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
              "name"
            ],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "1",
            "query": "min(last_10m):min:azure.network_expressroutecircuits.bgp_availability{env:prod,alert_band:critical,resource_type:azure_expressroute} by {name,peering_type} \u003c 100",
