            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · Unowned Resource Backlog\n**WHAT:** Unowned Resource Backlog: drift signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `platform-services` (platform / monitoring_platform, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Resources past the 14-day ownership SLA. Unowned means unactionable — an alert nobody receives is worse than no alert.\n\n**OWNER:** observability-platform · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Unowned Resource Backlog` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-ticket-sustained` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `observability-platform.prod.platform-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-platform-services` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Unowned Resource Backlog — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Unowned Resource Backlog — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Unowned Resource Backlog\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-platform-services`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
