            "id": "314408824",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Host CPU Baseline Deviation\n**WHAT:** Replaces \"CPU \u003e 80%\". A batch node at 95% on schedule is healthy; an API node at 55% when it normally runs at 20% is not. On its own this is a P3 diagnostic signal; it only becomes a page through event correlation with a service-level symptom.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `compute-platform` (infrastructure / host, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal deviated from its own learned baseline by more than the configured number of deviations — not because it crossed a fixed number.\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Host CPU Baseline Deviation` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-host` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `compute.prod.compute-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-infra-compute-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Host CPU Baseline Deviation — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Host CPU Baseline Deviation — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Host CPU Baseline Deviation\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-infra-compute-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "1",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][prod][infrastructure] Host CPU Baseline Deviation (standard)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
              "cluster"
            ],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "avg(last_30m):anomalies(avg:system.cpu.user{env:prod,alert_band:standard} by {cluster,host}, 'agile', 3, direction='above') \u003e= 1",
