          "index_key": "prod.standard.saas.saas-quota-forecast",
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "assets": [
              {
                "category": "runbook",
                "name": "SaaS API Quota Exhaustion Forecast",
                "resource_key": "15298679",
                "resource_type": "notebook",
                "url": "https://app.datadoghq.com/notebook/15298679"
              }
            ],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314408876",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · SaaS API Quota Exhaustion Forecast\n**WHAT:** Vendor API quotas reset on their calendar, not ours, and exhausting one mid-month is a self-inflicted outage with days of warning.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `external-dependencies` (saas / saas_vendor, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Extrapolating the recent trend, this resource is projected to cross its limit inside the forecast horizon. It has not crossed it yet — that is the point.\n**OWNER:** sre · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `SaaS API Quota Exhaustion Forecast` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-capacity-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `saas-dependency.prod.external-dependencies` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-external-dependency` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## SaaS API Quota Exhaustion Forecast — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## SaaS API Quota Exhaustion Forecast — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · SaaS API Quota Exhaustion Forecast\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-external-dependency`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "0.9",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "0.8",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][prod][saas] SaaS API Quota Exhaustion Forecast (standard)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "max(next_1d):forecast(sum:acme.saas.api_calls{env:prod,alert_band:standard} by {service}.as_count() / avg:acme.saas.api_quota{env:prod,alert_band:standard} by {service}, 'linear', 1, interval='60m', history='1w') \u003e 0.9",
            "renotify_interval": 120,
            "renotify_occurrences": 3,
            "renotify_statuses": [
              "alert"
            ],
            "require_full_window": false,
            "restricted_roles": null,
            "scheduling_options": [],
