            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · External Endpoint Latency Degradation\n**WHAT:** External Endpoint Latency Degradation: latency signal detected by rate_of_change analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `external-dependencies` (saas / synthetic_check, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal changed faster than the configured percentage relative to its own recent history. Speed of degradation, not absolute level.\n**OWNER:** sre · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `External Endpoint Latency Degradation` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-external-endpoint` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `external-endpoint.prod.external-dependencies` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-external-dependency` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## External Endpoint Latency Degradation — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## External Endpoint Latency Degradation — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · External Endpoint Latency Degradation\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-external-dependency`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
