            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Authentication Failure Anomaly\n**WHAT:** Weekly seasonality matters here: Monday morning login failures are normal, the same volume at 03:00 Sunday is not.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `security-telemetry` (security / identity_provider, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal deviated from its learned SEASONAL baseline (same hour, same day of week), so normal daily and weekly cycles are already accounted for.\n**OWNER:** security · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Authentication Failure Anomaly` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-security-control` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `identity-security.prod.security-telemetry` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-security-telemetry` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Authentication Failure Anomaly — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Authentication Failure Anomaly — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Authentication Failure Anomaly\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-security-telemetry`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "1",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
