            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · VM CPU Ready Contention\n**WHAT:** VM CPU Ready Contention: saturation signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `virtualization-platform` (vmware / esxi_host, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** CPU Ready above 10% is VMware's own published contention threshold — a vendor-defined operational boundary.\n\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `VM CPU Ready Contention` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-vmware` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `virtualization.prod.virtualization-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-vmware-cluster-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## VM CPU Ready Contention — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## VM CPU Ready Contention — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · VM CPU Ready Contention\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-vmware-cluster-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
